WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.860
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:12.990
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.250
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.750
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.300
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:34.140
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.310
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.150
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:45.070
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:52.530
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.540
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.960
Won't go away

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.790
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.930
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:38.280
We... came from the Japan of the 21st Century.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.210
Tubes one and two, loaded in! Opening hatch.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.670
Don't blame me.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:56.090
Blame your bad luck for having stopped your ship in a place like this.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:03.930
So that means, in that era, Japan still exists?

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:10.360
Mirai's Battle

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:15.400
The Empire of Japan continues to exist in the 21st Century?

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.570
So that must mean...

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.200
America and Japan were able to negotiate...

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.200
...a peace treaty with a favorable outcome, early in the war.

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.910
An early peace treaty?

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.960
I'm aware of Japan's precarious situation.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:34.250
Honestly, there is no other way for her to survive, aside from such a treaty.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:36.630
Hold it right there!

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.880
So you believe everything we said?!

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:43.220
Let me tell you something else! Japan has...!

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.140
That's enough.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:49.730
I'm Captain Umezu.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.270
Rest assured that this country will not be destroyed.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:57.360
Knowing that should be enough, right, Lieutenant Kusaka?

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:01.570
It is my honor to meet the highest-ranking officer of this ship.

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:02.740
Captain Umezu.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.870
Tubes one and two, ready to fire.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:12.750
Fire!

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.340
Torpedoes detected! 210 degrees!

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.930
High speed approach!

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.890
Torpedoes detected!

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:28.390
80 degrees left! Speed 44 knots, distance 3200!

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.810
2 minutes 10 seconds to impact!

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.230
- What?
- Oh, no!

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.730
T-Torpedoes?!

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.320
Start the engines!

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.610
Prepare for evasive action!

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.400
Evade them just like in the drills!

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.280
Aye aye, sir!

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:45.620
All sections, battle stations!

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:52.000
All hands on standby! Sonar at the ready!

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.040
We've got no time to waste!

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:01.380
Hey, hey! A torpedo? You can't be serious?!

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:08.060
Sonar to CIC, why wasn't this detected earlier?!

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.560
They were hidden amidst...

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.850
...the surface duct where we had difficulty detecting them.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:15.520
We also have insufficient oceanographic data for this region!

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.480
You idiot! This is the result of insufficient training!

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.150
I'm sorry, sir.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.610
Distance!

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.030
Distance 2000!

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.160
I'm having trouble spotting them, due to the reflective surface!

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.870
Torpedo wakes sighted!

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:30.080
Hurry back to the medical room!

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:39.170
What are you doing?! There are torpedoes headed this way!

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:45.680
I must see with my own eyes what this ship is capable of during a battle.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.680
Being a soldier myself, I can understand your interest.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.770
But your curiosity might just cost you your life.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:02.690
Main engine, startup okay!

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.280
Release the brake! All ahead full!

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.950
All ahead full!

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.880
Target ship starting up!

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.090
I've never heard of such engine noise before!

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:29.390
Starting up? So their ship wasn't malfunctioning?

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:30.720
Given their condition,

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:33.470
it should've taken them at least half a day to get moving.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.440
Five seconds to impact.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.900
Dodge them!

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.530
Prepare for impact!

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:50.240
That did it!

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:53.870
Bridge to CIC!

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:56.910
Transmit data on the origin of those torpedoes!

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.250
Bearing 240!

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:01.500
Distance 3800.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.840
W-We're dead meat.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:14.180
It's only been 30 seconds since they started their engines...

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:18.020
The Japanese... have such a superb ship?

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:29.820
Launch tubes three and four now!

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:32.280
Follow with five and six.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.830
Spread them out so that we'll hit them no matter what!

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.960
Aye, sir!

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.460
Tubes three, four, five and six. Opening hatch.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:50.890
Fire!

00:06:55.430 --> 00:07:01.190
Bearing 240 degrees. Distance 3700. Depth 10.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:02.190
Oguri!

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:03.690
Hard to starboard!

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.150
What incredible maneuverability.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.040
We'll be okay.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.380
Mirai will be able to evade their attacks.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:27.760
Oguri, I'm counting on you.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.130
So what if we change history?

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:32.550
Either way, we still can't go back.

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:34.720
New torpedo echoes detected!

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.770
Four in total, spreading out from port!

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.730
Bring it all on.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:40.810
What should we do?

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:43.480
Don't panic. Go back 10 degrees!

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:49.650
Do you honestly... want to see... our power?

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.040
Y-You asked for it...

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:04.460
Attacking us... in the first place.

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:11.380
I'm gonna... take you down!

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.380
Distance 3000 yards!

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.550
Before you take me!

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:21.850
We're hit? No...

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:31.400
A rocket...?

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.490
"VLS: Vertical Launching System"

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.490
Front deck VLS open.

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:41.370
"ASROC: Anti-Submarine Rocket"

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.750
ASROC fired.

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:42.250
What?!

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:44.540
It's heading for the point where the tubes were launched!

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.670
Who pressed that button?!

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:52.050
Yonekura!

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.090
You idiot!

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:55.300
Were you planning to start a war at your own discretion?

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:58.890
If we don't fight back, they'll finish us first, Weapons Officer!

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.980
Bridge to CIC, who gave the command to fire?!

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:05.900
I want a report, immediately!

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.940
Report the incident as human error!

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:14.950
And throw that guy out of CIC!

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:20.700
Two out of four torpedoes are 1000 yards from the ship!

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:26.960
Yanagi! Are those Japanese torpedoes or American?!

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:30.960
US Navy torpedo, Mark 14. No mistake about it.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:33.630
The Japanese Navy uses oxygen torpedoes,

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:35.590
which don't leave trails behind.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:39.640
Those that I saw earlier had a carbon dioxide discharge.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.600
Discharge trails visible! Give me the bearings!

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:46.270
130 degrees starboard! Relative speed about 5 knots!

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:48.100
Hard to starboard!

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:51.860
Distance 50.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.860
30!

00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.450
We've dodged them!

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.870
Not yet! Two more to go! Confirm their course!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.910
Two trails! Widening on approach!

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.920
- Distance 300!
- Turn the rudder back!

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:13.050
Distance 1500 yards!

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:19.550
Time to impact in five, four, three, two, one!

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:26.180
All torpedoes evaded! Receding behind!

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.990
What's that? A parachute?

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:55.750
Captain! A seeker is approaching.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:58.720
A seeker... what the...?

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:02.470
Are you saying... it has on board sonar?!

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:06.220
No doubt about it! A seeker is fast approaching!

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:10.900
How could Japan have something that the Royal Navy is still developing?

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:17.230
Hard starboard! All ahead full!

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.960
ASROC, in pursuit of target.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.130
Nothing detected on ES!

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:43.300
That submarine must have gathered a lot of data on our ship.

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:47.060
Such as our mobility when we dodged those torpedoes.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:50.640
They'll be reporting all this to the US Navy as soon as they're back at base.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.440
If we leave them be,

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:56.270
they'll continue to pursue us and launch endless attacks.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:59.740
At this rate, the safety and the secrecy of this ship...

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.700
...will be...

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.870
Even if they report us, we've still got options.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:13.500
But, if we sink a ship that is not meant to be sunk,

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:16.040
there'll be no turning back.

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:24.050
Bridge, CIC.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:27.470
Captain, permission request for ASROC self-destruct.

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:30.640
- Executive Officer.
- Sir?

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:34.900
Is America... an enemy to all of us here?

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:37.560
Nothing detected on water surface! No abnormalities!

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:42.030
Identifying our attackers as a direct threat to our mission...

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:46.280
...and eliminating them is the basis of self-defense, correct?

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:50.160
180 degrees! 7600 yards! No response from the Sonar System!

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:53.960
Alright then. Relay your orders please.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.500
Sir!

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.340
CIC to Bridge!

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:02.010
Maintain current course and await instructions.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:03.170
What?!

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:14.230
The approaching object's a torpedo!

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:15.980
A seeker from a torpedo?!

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:18.150
What are you talking about?!

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:21.360
That can't be. No torpedo has sonar capabilities...

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:54.220
Torpedo impact in 10 seconds!

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:58.850
Kikuchi! Initiate self-destruct!

00:13:59.060 --> 00:13:59.940
Aye-aye!

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:16.620
Sonar, are you able to pick up the engine of the submarine?

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.290
I don't hear its engine but...

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:22.500
I can hear the sub creaking and discharging compressed air.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:25.340
Looks like it's surfacing rapidly.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:29.720
I want to think that this was the best available option...

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.010
...despite the circumstances.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:37.310
But, we might have been pushed closer to the edge again.

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:38.600
Yeah.

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:02.040
Captain,

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:04.460
the watertight bulkhead is cracked,

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:08.800
and it will take time for us to fix the damaged communication antenna.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:11.220
Once the repairs are done, we'll commence...

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:12.680
We'll retreat.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:16.220
We must retreat to Pearl Harbor.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:21.190
We gotta get this information back to HQ.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:25.440
As much as I don't wanna believe it.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:30.820
It looks like Japan has for themselves some sort of new super weapon.

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:32.360
Darn.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:43.790
How are you feeling? Are you alright?

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:51.550
Are you satisfied now? So what do you think?

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:56.100
Is this part of our god's plan? Or a will of the devil?

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:57.680
No matter how you look at it,

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:01.270
this battle has surpassed the imaginations of the people from this era.

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:07.820
This is a battle of the 21st Century.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.910
Reporting, sir!

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:21.350
Fourth Torpedo Division, Lieutenant Tsuda,

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:23.600
reporting as ordered!

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:28.400
You've done well.

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:39.580
Sir Admiral Nagumo is scheduled to arrive...

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:43.700
...aboard the Light Cruiser Nagayori and board the Yamato at 1800 hours.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.330
He will deliver the results from the battle at Midway.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:48.880
Here is the report I've drafted, sir.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.670
Please, have a seat.

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:54.920
Thank you very much.

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:59.970
The junior officers and soldiers must be unhappy...

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:02.060
...that we have yet to launch a counter attack, no?

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:04.020
Yes... No!

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:08.650
Why haven't we brought the Yamato out to avenge the lost carriers?

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:13.320
They must think the Commander in Chief is a cowardly man, right?

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.690
No, sir! No one thinks that way.

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:18.490
That's alright. Let them complain.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:22.200
They need to release their discontent.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:25.420
Isoroku Yamamoto
Combined Fleet Commander in Chief

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:24.910
It is no fault of theirs, anyway.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:29.580
The commander had been very much against launching war on America,

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:32.500
yet he initiated the attack on Pearl Harbour.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:38.340
What exactly does he feel, about the defeat at Midway?

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:42.850
From the look on your face, I can read what's on your mind.

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:47.810
It is most regrettable that Yamaguchi and Captain Kaku...

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:49.440
...had to go down with their ships.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:53.360
Do give my regards to Admiral Nagumo and remind him that...

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:57.070
...I alone, shall bear the full responsibility,

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:59.490
and tell him not to act rashly.

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:04.370
Sir,

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:07.200
if the Commander in Chief decides to commit hara-kiri,

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:10.460
then all officers of the Striking Force will like to follow suit!

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.710
Listen, rumor has it that...

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:18.010
...I have been given the nickname 'god of war'.

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:21.130
How does an immortal go about dying?

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:26.470
It takes three years to build a flight carrier.

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:29.480
A pilot's training takes between five to ten years.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:33.730
However, the cultivation of a superb leader...

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:36.320
...cannot be measured by time.

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:43.070
Right now, Japan cannot afford to have leaders slitting their bellies at whim.

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:47.540
I apologize for what I've said!

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:50.540
By the way,

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:55.040
there is still no news of Lieutenant Kusaka, I presume?

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:57.960
Yes. He is still missing.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:00.630
He left the Kirishima in a seaplane.

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:03.140
We still have no news of him.

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:06.600
I really hope he's still alive.

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.890
Contrary to his youthful appearance,

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:11.940
he never displayed the rashness common to his peers.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:14.480
He is a calm and composed soldier,

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:16.860
a rarity among military personnel in this era, indeed.

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:20.280
Lieutenant Kusaka may seem cold,

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:23.860
but he is an Imperial Navy Soldier with a heart full of patriotism.

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:26.950
Regardless of what manner of crisis he is faced with,

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:32.460
I firmly believe he would deny himself death, till his mission is complete.

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:35.880
As expected, that ship's data isn't recorded in here.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:39.170
That ship? What are you referring to?

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:43.380
It was the night before the Battle of Midway.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:48.810
An unidentified ship appeared, right before Yamato,

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:51.060
in the midst of a thick fog.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:55.520
What's more, she bore our navy flag.

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:59.780
It had a peculiar structure, and such acceleration mobility...

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:02.070
...as never seen before.

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:04.400
After evading our destroyers...

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:07.990
...without spewing even a single cloud of black smoke, it disappeared.

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:12.830
Probably a US ship in disguise?

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:15.000
They could have violated the rules of the war.

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:18.540
Many on this ship have had the same opinion,

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:21.090
but I strongly doubt it's the case.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:26.340
First of all, the US neither undertakes nor needs a disguise.

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:30.220
Oops, someone's likely to accuse me of favoring the US again.

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:33.560
Either way, we're faced with a new threat.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:37.230
Will you channel your efforts into data retrieval on this matter?

00:21:38.270 --> 00:21:39.230
Yes, sir!

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:43.190
It's just a hunch,

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:45.570
but I feel that this ship...

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:48.530
might alter the course of situation in the Pacific Ocean,

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:50.950
Or that of the whole world.

00:22:09.640 --> 00:22:17.190
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.320 --> 00:22:22.430
Just peacefully

00:22:21.890 --> 00:22:34.200
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.370 --> 00:22:47.120
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.620 --> 00:22:53.720
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:59.800
I kept on praying

00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:11.640
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.480 --> 00:23:27.320
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.340 --> 00:23:43.350
Kikuchi! It'll be your fault if Satake goes down!

00:23:43.680 --> 00:23:46.180
The Mirai is the only country we have now!

00:23:46.180 --> 00:23:48.850
We cannot just standby and allow it to be taken over!

00:23:48.980 --> 00:23:52.230
No one should live life like a dead person.

00:23:52.230 --> 00:23:53.860
We are alive, and we should live each day.

00:23:53.860 --> 00:23:56.690
I'm not giving up! If we change the course of history,

00:23:56.690 --> 00:23:58.990
the 21st century as we know it may cease to exist!

00:23:58.990 --> 00:24:00.490
This is the epiphany of my life.

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:04.870
Next Episode: Kusaka's Choice

00:24:00.490 --> 00:24:04.580
I've lived thirty-two years, just to understand this.

00:24:04.870 --> 00:24:09.880
This story is purely fiction. The names of the
characters and organizations that appear have no
connections with actual people and organizations.
